<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beleheb Tz'i</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1524">1524</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beleheb Tz'i was one of the leading kings of the K'iche' Maya kingdom in highland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> at the time of the Spanish conquest. After defeating the K'iche' near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quetzaltenango">Quetzaltenango</a> in 1524, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a> accused Beleheb Tz'i and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxib-keh">Oxib Keh</a> of plotting against him and had them burnt alive at their capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qumarkaj">Q'umarkaj</a>, which the Spanish then destroyed.</p></div>
